---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Conclave AX — AI work with a clear path to done"
  description="Conclave AX coordinates AI and tool work across your Workspace, Hosts, Workers, and Accounts."
>
  <section class="hero" id="product">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">A clearer way to direct AI work</div>
      <h1>Move from an idea to evidence you can trust.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Conclave AX gives teams one place to ask, direct, review, and understand
        AI-powered work—while keeping execution close to the machines and accounts
        that make it possible.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button-primary" href="https://app.conclaveax.com">Open Conclave AX</a>
        <a class="button-secondary" href="/how-it-works/">See how it works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="architecture-card" aria-label="Conclave AX architecture">
      <div class="eyebrow">The simple picture</div>
      <p>Cloud coordinates. Host provides the machine. Workers provide capability.</p>
      <div class="flow">
        <span>Conclave AX</span>
        <span>Conclave Cloud</span>
        <span>Conclave Host</span>
        <span>Worker</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Designed for real work</div>
    <h2>Less black box. More useful control.</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      Your work stays organized in Workspaces and Projects. Progress, artifacts,
      findings, and verification become part of the result—not scattered afterthoughts.
    </p>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card"><h3>Direct the work</h3><p>Describe the outcome. Conclave AX coordinates the steps and the people or Workers involved.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Keep capability close</h3><p>A Conclave Host runs on your machine and supervises the Workers you choose to use.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>See what happened</h3><p>Inspect progress, evidence, artifacts, and usage without relying on a model's summary alone.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
